SUMMARY:Cat Gap Trail to John Rock Loop - 6 Miles\, 1000 Ft
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 6 Miles\, 1000 Ft
  elevation gain\n* Carpool meeting time is 9:00 at the Mills River Ingles 
 by the gas pumps.\n* Hike starts at 9:30\n* Sign up starts Friday at 5pm\n
 \nThis hike is a special request from Josef. This is a nice loop that star
 ts at the Fish Hatchery and goes up to John Rock via the Cat Gap Looooop t
 rail. We will have a snack there before heading back down and taking a qui
 ck stop at Cedar Rock Falls. We will do a moderate pace of about 2.7 mph b
 ut stop for breaks as needed.\n\nThere will be an opportunity to stop at a
  brewery on the way back.\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will meet at the Mill River I
 ngles by the gas pumps at 9:00. Please be there a little early so we can l
 eave at 9:00 for the trailhead. If you plan to meet us at the Fish Hatcher
 y-John Rock trailhead\, plan to be there by 9:30 but parking is very limit
 ed due to construction so please try to carpool unless you are coming from
  a different direction.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and post a 
 cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of precipit
 ation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 9:00 AM 
 the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to text or cal
 l me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis As
 heville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation
  to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for their own s
 afety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditio
 ning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and p
 roperty. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure
  your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsibil
 ity for any injuries\, damages\, or losses
