BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_315015172@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260530T040440Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260603T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260603T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Pow
 hatan Rec Area\nRSVP's don't open until 6PM Sunday night.\nWeather: or not
 \, I'll let you know if it's raining\, and/or cancelled.\nI did this hike 
 series for many years before 2022\, but I did it as a high-speed hike\, an
 d I am now doing it as a moderate speed hike. This is a numbers limited ev
 ent and I expect people who sign-up to show up. Late cancellations\, and t
 hose that don't show up are bumping other interested hikers\, and they wil
 l not be allowed on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\, I will try to post a
  hike most weeks\, and for days Tue or Wed\, distance\, and start location
 \, like switching between Hard Times trail-head and Bent Creek River Park\
 , may change.\nThe current route is about 5.5 miles.\nPlease folks\, this 
 is intended as a moderate paced hike\, and we'd like all attendees to keep
  up with the hike leader(s). This hike is intended as a workout hike for p
 eople to get in condition to do weekend hikes.\nModerate paced means 22-24
  min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take breaks\, take in views
 \, or snap photos along the way. Please make sure you're able to keep up w
 ith the group. This hike has always served as a good chance to get exercis
 e during the week\, meet new people\, and create interest for weekend enjo
 yment hikes. It's a great introduction to the AHG family.\nNo need to RSVP
  "No" or "not attending" unless changing from a "Yes."\nPlease read the fu
 ll description before RSVPing\, and only sign up if you are sure you can g
 o. Thanks in advance for keeping your RSVP up-to-date and not being a last
 -minute cancellation or no-show. This is an ongoing issue with Meetups and
  often keeps people on waitlists from being able to attend our hikes.\nHar
 d Times Trailhead near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow signs off of Brevard
  Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is Bent Creek Ranch Rd. t
 o Wesley Branch Rd. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan until you come to Hard T
 imes Trailhead on your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very clearly marked. Parkin
 g is very limited at the trailhead but there’s a paved pull-off just bef
 ore the Hard Times trailhead and more parking just beyond at the Ledford B
 ranch trailhead. We will access Bent Creek forest by way of Hard Times Tra
 il and do some combination of loop and out and back.\nArrive at the trailh
 ead BY 6:00. Because it is a weeknight hike\, we are unable to wait for la
 tecomers\, fighting daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are running behind\, please
  post a comment on this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There is no cell service a
 t the parking lot\, so if we don't have any advance notice of you running 
 late by 5:45\, we can't get any notifications at the trailhead and we will
  not wait for you.\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarely do we get much late
 r than that.\n• Wear closed-toed footwear appropriate for hiking. The tr
 ail will consist of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mulch.\n• Bring plent
 y of water.\n• Bring rain gear if a chance of rain is in the forecast.\n
 Headlamps suggested\n• Dogs on leashes the whole time are welcome. This 
 is an active mountain bike area and it can get messy with dogs running loo
 se among hikers and mountain bikers.\nPlease make sure to keep your RSVP u
 p-to-date. You don't want to be "that person" who cancels last minute or n
 o-shows and keeps someone from joining in if there's a waitlist. Thanks fo
 r your consideration - it is appreciated!\nFeel free to post questions not
  covered in this description in the comments section.\nThanks - we'll see 
 you on the trail!\nDisclaimer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity inv
 olves hiking on city streets that may have traffic and/or natural trails w
 ith roots\, rocks\, and steep sections. Participants are responsible for t
 heir safety on streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunte
 er and not a professional guide. The function of the organizer is only to 
 organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknow
 ledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injurie
 s\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated
  with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meet
 up terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315015172
 /
